<body>
<h1>Why the Sky is Blue</h1>
<div class="container">
  <div class="column">
<h2>For a 3-year-old toddler</h2>
<p>The sky looks blue because the sunlight that comes from the sun hits tiny bits in the air and makes the blue light bounce around more than the other colors. It's like when you shine a flashlight through a glass of water with a little milk in it—everything looks bluish!</p>

<h2>For a high school teenager</h2>
<p>The sky appears blue due to Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight is made of many colors, each with different wavelengths. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen). Shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) are scattered much more efficiently than longer wavelengths (red, orange). Our eyes are more sensitive to blue than violet, and some violet light is absorbed by the upper atmosphere, so we perceive the sky as blue.</p>

<h2>For a physics PhD</h2>
<p>The blue color of the sky results from elastic scattering of solar radiation by atmospheric constituents, primarily described by Rayleigh scattering theory. The scattering cross-section scales as \(\sigma \propto \lambda^{-4}\), leading to preferential scattering of shorter wavelengths. The incident solar spectrum, approximated as a blackbody at ~5778 K, peaks in the green, but after integrating the scattered intensity over the solid angle and weighting by the photopic response of the human eye, the dominant perceived color is blue (~450–495 nm). Corrections for Mie scattering from aerosols and the wavelength-dependent absorption by ozone (Chappuis bands) slightly modify the hue, especially near the horizon. Additionally, the polarization of scattered light follows a sinusoidal pattern with scattering angle, providing a diagnostic tool for atmospheric studies.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="column">
<h2>对于3岁的幼儿</h2>
<p>天空看起来是蓝色的，因为来自太阳的阳光击中空气中的微小颗粒，使蓝光比其他颜色更多地四处反射。就像当你用手电筒照射一杯加入少量牛奶的水时——一切看起来都带蓝色！</p>

<h2>对于高中生</h2>
<p>天空呈蓝色是由于瑞利散射。阳光由许多不同波长的颜色组成。当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会与气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）碰撞。较短波长的光（蓝色和紫色）散射得比较长波长的光（红色、橙色）更有效。我们的眼睛对蓝光比对紫光更敏感，而且一些紫光被上层大气吸收，因此我们感知到天空是蓝色的。</p>

<h2>对于物理学博士</h2>
<p>天空的蓝色来源于大气成分对太阳辐射的弹性散射，主要由瑞利散射理论描述。散射截面与波长的四次方成反比（\(\sigma \propto \lambda^{-4}\)），导致较短波长的光被更优先散射。入射太阳光谱近似为约5778 K的黑体，其峰值位于绿光区域，但在将散射强度在立体角上积分并根据人眼的光opic响应进行加权后，主导感知颜色为蓝色（约450–495 nm）。艾ROSOSOL溶胶的米散射以及臭氧（Chappuis带）的波长依赖性吸收的校正会略微改变色调，尤其是在地平线附近。此外，散射光的偏振随着散射角度呈正弦变化，这为大气研究提供了诊断工具。</p>
